PART 2: C Program to Calculate Sum of Digits (5 marks)

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int num, temp, digit, sum = 0;

    printf("Enter an integer number: ");
    scanf("%d", &num);

    temp = num;  // Store original number
    if (temp < 0)
        temp = -temp;  // Handle negative numbers

    while (temp != 0) {
        digit = temp % 10;   // Extract last digit
        sum = sum + digit;   // Add digit to sum
        temp = temp / 10;    // Remove last digit
    }

    printf("Sum of digits of %d = %d\n", num, sum);

    return 0;
}

Sample Output:
Enter an integer number: 1234
Sum of digits of 1234 = 10

Step-by-step trace for input 1234:
Iteration 1: digit = 1234 % 10 = 4, sum = 4,  temp = 123
Iteration 2: digit = 123  % 10 = 3, sum = 7,  temp = 12
Iteration 3: digit = 12   % 10 = 2, sum = 9,  temp = 1
Iteration 4: digit = 1    % 10 = 1, sum = 10, temp = 0
Loop ends. Sum = 10

PART 1: What is an Array? (2 marks)

Definition:
An array is a collection of elements of the same data type stored in contiguous memory locations, accessed using a common name and an index.

Key Points:
1. All elements must be of the same data type.
2. Elements are stored in consecutive memory locations.
3. Each element is accessed using its index (starting from 0).
4. Array size must be declared at the time of definition (in static arrays).

Syntax: data_type array_name[size];
Example: int marks[5]; → stores 5 integers

